WEBVTT

00:00:14.570 --> 00:00:16.160
Polar Bear's Café

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:20.450
Polar Bear's Café

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:34.940
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:01:31.480 --> 00:01:34.380
A Magazine Interview Comes By!

00:01:39.660 --> 00:01:42.440
I wonder why it's not going well.

00:01:42.440 --> 00:01:45.370
Huh? What? 
Oh, that.

00:01:46.220 --> 00:01:47.800
Parallel parking?

00:01:49.830 --> 00:01:51.100
No!

00:01:51.100 --> 00:01:53.510
So you're able to do it now?

00:01:54.540 --> 00:01:57.070
No, not quite yet...

00:01:57.070 --> 00:01:58.050
But that's not it!

00:01:58.810 --> 00:02:01.710
I'm talking about my date.

00:02:01.710 --> 00:02:03.760
I don't know how to ask someone out.

00:02:04.370 --> 00:02:06.070
Why don't you just meet 
up with her and ask?

00:02:06.070 --> 00:02:09.060
That's the problem!
I can't bring myself to do it.

00:02:09.910 --> 00:02:11.010
Why?

00:02:13.920 --> 00:02:14.610
Never mind.

00:02:15.230 --> 00:02:17.700
It was a mistake to ask you, Panda.

00:02:18.990 --> 00:02:20.480
Mr. Polar Bear!

00:02:22.020 --> 00:02:24.740
Sorry! We're a little late!

00:02:25.890 --> 00:02:27.570
Who might you be?

00:02:27.570 --> 00:02:29.290
They're here for the piece.

00:02:29.290 --> 00:02:30.250
Piece?

00:02:30.670 --> 00:02:32.380
We talked about it yesterday.

00:02:32.860 --> 00:02:34.750
Yes, I know.

00:02:34.750 --> 00:02:37.800
Interview in progress. 
Please come again.

00:02:37.800 --> 00:02:40.260
Writer:
Ohsaki Mayumi

00:02:38.460 --> 00:02:40.690
Hi, I'm a writer 
for "Furafura Walker Monthly."

00:02:40.690 --> 00:02:42.320
My name is Ohsaki.

00:02:42.320 --> 00:02:43.740
Nice to meet you.

00:02:45.560 --> 00:02:46.760
Is something wrong?

00:02:46.760 --> 00:02:50.850
Um, well, our editor-in-chief 
should be here already.

00:02:51.080 --> 00:02:52.650
Editor-in-chief?

00:02:53.180 --> 00:02:56.070
I don't believe he's here yet.

00:02:56.430 --> 00:02:59.530
I see. I wonder what happened.

00:03:00.310 --> 00:03:02.690
Actually, the person who wanted to

00:03:02.690 --> 00:03:06.040
cover this place was 
our editor-in-chief.

00:03:08.030 --> 00:03:09.960
He's got a knack for finding

00:03:09.960 --> 00:03:13.800
hole-in-the-wall cafés 
and unique open cafés.

00:03:13.800 --> 00:03:18.130
Our magazine pretty much 
runs on his intuition.

00:03:18.770 --> 00:03:20.030
Did you hear?

00:03:20.030 --> 00:03:21.790
It's a piece for a magazine.

00:03:22.170 --> 00:03:23.370
Piece?

00:03:23.370 --> 00:03:24.920
They're probably going 
to do a few interviews

00:03:24.920 --> 00:03:26.600
and take a lot of pictures.

00:03:28.090 --> 00:03:31.060
Interviews? Pictures?

00:03:31.060 --> 00:03:35.020
Exclusive 
Interview

00:03:31.060 --> 00:03:35.020
The 
Panda 
that 
knows 
change.

00:03:31.060 --> 00:03:35.020
A 
memorable 
time

00:03:36.900 --> 00:03:39.260
I wonder if I'll get fan mail.

00:03:40.290 --> 00:03:42.550
The piece isn't about you, Panda.

00:03:43.060 --> 00:03:46.490
If they interview customers, 
our pictures will be in the magazine.

00:03:47.620 --> 00:03:49.240
That's not okay!

00:03:49.480 --> 00:03:53.100
I'm not photogenic at all!

00:03:53.530 --> 00:03:57.230
Well then, let's begin our interview.

00:03:58.970 --> 00:04:03.650
First, we'd like to know how it all began.

00:04:06.110 --> 00:04:07.640
How it all began <i>(ikisatsu)</i>...

00:04:11.910 --> 00:04:13.190
That would be an artistic 
masterpiece <i>(rikisaku)</i>.

00:04:14.280 --> 00:04:15.720
That would be printing<i> (insatsu)</i>.

00:04:17.390 --> 00:04:19.080
That would be a police 
officer<i> (keisatsu)</i>.

00:04:19.840 --> 00:04:21.030
That would be ticket 
punching<i> (kaisatsu)</i>.

00:04:21.850 --> 00:04:24.450
U-Um... those puns...

00:04:28.050 --> 00:04:29.590
That would be a greeting<i> (aisatsu)</i>!

00:04:29.590 --> 00:04:31.890
Way to step right in, Mr. Editor!

00:04:33.340 --> 00:04:36.670
The owner is a 
pun-loving, nice guy.

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:39.400
Mr. Editor?

00:04:39.400 --> 00:04:42.630
Yes, he's our editor-in-chief, 
Mr. Shoebill.

00:04:44.140 --> 00:04:47.810
Right? Your lead was amazing this time!

00:04:50.460 --> 00:04:54.310
He says that this café 
is absolutely amazing.

00:04:54.310 --> 00:04:55.710
I see.

00:04:56.520 --> 00:05:00.980
So, once again, why did you 
decide to open this café?

00:05:03.170 --> 00:05:05.810
I guess she's going to 
ask him after all.

00:05:05.810 --> 00:05:07.120
Why?

00:05:07.400 --> 00:05:09.970
It's a rather long story,

00:05:09.970 --> 00:05:13.110
but I was born near the
 Hudson Bay in Canada.

00:05:19.230 --> 00:05:24.030
I was the youngest of triplets, 
and the smallest.

00:05:25.300 --> 00:05:28.600
Whenever my mom would 
go look for food,

00:05:28.600 --> 00:05:31.490
I would always fall behind.

00:05:35.480 --> 00:05:38.100
Then, one day, during a snowstorm,

00:05:39.020 --> 00:05:43.130
I was completely separated 
from my family.

00:05:58.990 --> 00:06:00.960
After the storm passed,

00:06:05.650 --> 00:06:09.510
I couldn't see my mom 
or siblings anywhere.

00:06:11.910 --> 00:06:15.520
I called out for them, 
but there was no answer.

00:06:16.890 --> 00:06:18.780
And then, I noticed...

00:06:20.080 --> 00:06:23.610
the piece of ice I was 
on was floating away.

00:06:25.470 --> 00:06:30.380
I was all alone and drifting out to sea.

00:06:32.490 --> 00:06:36.310
For days... and days...

00:06:38.220 --> 00:06:41.320
W-What happened after that?

00:06:42.080 --> 00:06:46.540
When I'd gotten so hungry 
that I couldn't even move,

00:06:50.220 --> 00:06:54.840
I was rescued by a passing fisherman.

00:07:01.860 --> 00:07:07.190
After that, he left me in his parents' care.

00:07:07.190 --> 00:07:10.900
Seal Restaurant

00:07:07.580 --> 00:07:10.900
They ran a little restaurant

00:07:11.520 --> 00:07:13.870
and as I helped them out,

00:07:13.870 --> 00:07:16.830
I began to enjoy cooking.

00:07:17.770 --> 00:07:21.790
But that life didn't last long, either.

00:07:25.290 --> 00:07:33.180
I became so big that I couldn't 
stay at their house anymore.

00:07:34.330 --> 00:07:36.080
So I left the house,

00:07:36.900 --> 00:07:38.550
and opened this café.

00:07:39.350 --> 00:07:41.940
Cover 
Story

00:07:39.870 --> 00:07:41.970
I thought if I started a café,

00:07:41.970 --> 00:07:44.310
word would eventually get around,

00:07:44.760 --> 00:07:47.850
and I might be able to 
see my family again.

00:07:53.710 --> 00:07:55.210
Huh? What?

00:07:55.670 --> 00:07:57.830
I know, Mr. Editor!

00:07:57.830 --> 00:08:00.700
Just thinking about 
Mr. Polar Bear's suffering...

00:08:03.180 --> 00:08:04.770
Polar Bear...

00:08:07.780 --> 00:08:09.910
You've had it so hard!

00:08:12.860 --> 00:08:15.390
Have you seen your family yet?

00:08:15.390 --> 00:08:18.400
No, not yet.

00:08:19.110 --> 00:08:20.120
Huh?

00:08:21.300 --> 00:08:23.240
I thought you told me the other day

00:08:23.240 --> 00:08:26.470
that you quit your job at 
the construction company

00:08:26.470 --> 00:08:28.130
to open up the café.

00:08:36.130 --> 00:08:38.190
There's that version, too.

00:08:38.910 --> 00:08:40.410
You made that up?

00:08:40.900 --> 00:08:42.450
I warned you.

00:08:42.860 --> 00:08:46.170
Oh, so we can use whichever version we like.

00:08:46.170 --> 00:08:47.380
Nothing less from the nice guy.

00:08:48.290 --> 00:08:50.220
The next question...

00:08:56.770 --> 00:08:58.250
What's wrong, Mr. Editor?

00:09:06.120 --> 00:09:08.560
Oh, those flowers.

00:09:10.320 --> 00:09:12.860
Who did these fabulous arrangements?

00:09:13.510 --> 00:09:16.110
A local flower shop does it for us.

00:09:19.640 --> 00:09:20.910
Mr. Editor?

00:09:22.550 --> 00:09:24.360
Mr. Editor!

00:09:25.580 --> 00:09:27.970
Mr. Editor!

00:09:29.480 --> 00:09:30.750
Mr. Edit―

00:09:35.370 --> 00:09:36.720
This is...

00:09:38.340 --> 00:09:40.200
It's our very own vegetable garden.

00:09:40.200 --> 00:09:43.440
We grow the vegetables and 
herbs that we use in the café.

00:09:43.440 --> 00:09:45.510
You're amazing, Mr. Editor!

00:09:45.510 --> 00:09:47.500
You don't miss a thing.

00:09:49.190 --> 00:09:50.840
Hand-picked ingredients,

00:09:51.480 --> 00:09:53.330
beautiful scenery,

00:09:54.060 --> 00:09:55.940
ample seating,

00:09:57.150 --> 00:09:59.160
a polished exterior...

00:09:59.830 --> 00:10:02.620
You have such an amazing place.

00:10:02.620 --> 00:10:06.080
Would you be willing to share
 any recommendations you have?

00:10:06.770 --> 00:10:09.210
I recommend the large 
serving of bamboo grass!

00:10:09.210 --> 00:10:11.790
That's more like 
raw ingredients than food.

00:10:11.790 --> 00:10:16.630
Oh! I also recommend how it's right next 
to my house and easy to get to.

00:10:16.630 --> 00:10:18.550
That's just you, Panda.

00:10:18.550 --> 00:10:21.260
The ingredients and location 
are extraordinary.

00:10:21.710 --> 00:10:23.210
What else?

00:10:24.110 --> 00:10:25.980
The lunch pasta is popular.

00:10:27.280 --> 00:10:29.140
The one with anchovies.

00:10:29.730 --> 00:10:31.940
The one with spring vegetables, too.

00:10:32.460 --> 00:10:35.370
Why don't we make it for 
them since they're here?

00:10:51.990 --> 00:10:53.710
What do you think, Mr. Editor?

00:10:55.710 --> 00:10:57.720
Maybe he doesn't like pasta.

00:11:06.930 --> 00:11:09.280
That was quite dynamic.

00:11:12.920 --> 00:11:16.540
I see! He says it's very delicious!

00:11:16.540 --> 00:11:18.010
I see.

00:11:25.850 --> 00:11:29.290
What? That magazine's already out?

00:11:29.670 --> 00:11:31.780
Yup. I received a sample copy.

00:11:31.780 --> 00:11:34.010
Let me see, let me see!

00:11:34.410 --> 00:11:36.280
Oh, right here.

00:11:36.750 --> 00:11:39.720
Our

00:11:36.750 --> 00:11:39.720
Charismatic

00:11:36.750 --> 00:11:39.720
Editor-in-Chief

00:11:36.750 --> 00:11:39.720
Approves

00:11:39.720 --> 00:11:42.680
The owner is a pun-loving

00:11:39.720 --> 00:11:42.680
Nice Guy.

00:11:42.680 --> 00:11:45.640
Polished interior 
Calm surroundings

00:11:45.640 --> 00:11:48.600
Proficient in making exquisite cuisine 
with hand-picked ingredients

00:11:48.600 --> 00:11:51.560
The ultimate extravagance
Careful care in roasting
Authentic coffee

00:11:51.560 --> 00:11:54.520
Our Editor-in-chief's seal of approval!

00:11:51.560 --> 00:11:54.520
The popular lunch pasta
Even the ladies

00:11:55.660 --> 00:11:57.180
I'm not in it.

00:11:57.180 --> 00:11:58.360
I'm in it.

00:11:59.000 --> 00:12:00.490
It appears so.

00:12:00.490 --> 00:12:09.950
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:12:09.950 --> 00:12:14.920
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:12:11.490 --> 00:12:14.330
Salmon Hunter: Mr. Grizzly!

00:12:18.880 --> 00:12:20.590
In preparations

00:12:22.900 --> 00:12:24.300
Good morning.

00:12:24.640 --> 00:12:26.670
Good morning, Panda.

00:12:27.590 --> 00:12:28.600
Oh?

00:12:29.380 --> 00:12:31.420
What's all that for?

00:12:31.420 --> 00:12:32.980
I'm getting ready for a trip.

00:12:32.980 --> 00:12:35.510
You're going on a trip?

00:12:35.510 --> 00:12:36.800
What about the café?

00:12:36.800 --> 00:12:38.490
It's closed for the day.

00:12:38.490 --> 00:12:39.720
What?

00:12:39.720 --> 00:12:44.210
But I got up early, so I figured I 
could make it in time for breakfast.

00:12:44.210 --> 00:12:45.450
Sorry about that.

00:12:45.830 --> 00:12:47.410
Where are you going?

00:12:47.410 --> 00:12:48.810
Today...

00:12:50.270 --> 00:12:53.830
You better be ready, Polar Bear.

00:12:54.970 --> 00:12:56.880
Is this all your stuff?

00:12:56.880 --> 00:12:57.540
Yup.

00:12:58.160 --> 00:13:00.290
Good morning, Mr. Grizzly.

00:13:00.860 --> 00:13:01.460
Hey.

00:13:01.990 --> 00:13:04.470
Where are you two headed?

00:13:05.950 --> 00:13:08.530
We're gonna go get some ingredients.

00:13:08.530 --> 00:13:10.930
We're going to go excavate for 
some ingredients for cooking.

00:13:11.810 --> 00:13:14.490
Excavate? That sounds like fun!

00:13:14.490 --> 00:13:15.690
I wanna go, too.

00:13:15.690 --> 00:13:17.910
This ain't no game!

00:13:18.910 --> 00:13:22.150
Well, it is sort of like a field trip.

00:13:22.780 --> 00:13:23.650
Field trip?

00:13:24.190 --> 00:13:26.430
Will there be bamboo grass for snacks?

00:13:26.430 --> 00:13:27.870
Or maybe lunch?

00:13:27.870 --> 00:13:30.710
Hmm, that could be difficult.

00:13:30.710 --> 00:13:32.600
Seals are lunch, though.

00:13:35.600 --> 00:13:37.300
What about snacks?

00:13:37.300 --> 00:13:38.710
Maybe walruses.

00:13:41.120 --> 00:13:43.440
What the hell are you babbling about?

00:13:43.440 --> 00:13:44.280
Let's go!

00:13:44.280 --> 00:13:45.470
Hurry and get in!

00:13:49.880 --> 00:13:51.530
Hey, Polar Bear.

00:13:51.530 --> 00:13:53.640
What is it, Grizzly?

00:13:56.830 --> 00:13:58.880
Why the hell is he here?

00:13:58.880 --> 00:14:01.350
You told him to get in.

00:14:01.350 --> 00:14:02.990
That's not what I meant!

00:14:02.990 --> 00:14:05.110
It doesn't really matter.

00:14:06.780 --> 00:14:08.960
Hey, where are we going?

00:14:08.960 --> 00:14:10.040
To the mountains?

00:14:10.040 --> 00:14:11.330
Or maybe to the beach?

00:14:12.980 --> 00:14:16.290
There's lots of delicious bamboo 
grass in the mountains.

00:14:17.250 --> 00:14:20.820
And there're a lot of cute 
girls at the beach.

00:14:22.340 --> 00:14:23.630
We're going to the river.

00:14:31.760 --> 00:14:34.640
You want some 
for your café, right?

00:14:34.640 --> 00:14:38.250
Yup. It'd be great if 
we get a lot.

00:14:38.250 --> 00:14:40.350
It looks like there's quite a few.

00:14:48.610 --> 00:14:50.580
Oh, a fish.

00:14:50.580 --> 00:14:52.980
That would be our target.

00:14:53.930 --> 00:14:54.950
That?

00:14:55.410 --> 00:14:56.590
That's right.

00:14:57.130 --> 00:14:58.160
Salmon.

00:15:01.150 --> 00:15:02.480
What?

00:15:03.300 --> 00:15:06.970
I was imagining something 
more like bamboo shoots.

00:15:06.970 --> 00:15:08.470
If you don't want any, go home!

00:15:08.950 --> 00:15:12.180
This isn't an excavation at all.

00:15:12.180 --> 00:15:13.950
It's similar.

00:15:14.600 --> 00:15:16.430
Really?

00:15:16.930 --> 00:15:18.790
Good luck!

00:15:18.790 --> 00:15:21.640
Starting tomorrow, 
lunch at Polar Bear's Café

00:15:21.640 --> 00:15:24.030
is all riding on you, Grizzly.

00:15:25.440 --> 00:15:28.820
Jeez, relying on me to 
do all your work.

00:15:30.960 --> 00:15:33.210
Ooh, how's he going to catch it?

00:15:58.570 --> 00:16:00.270
There's one!

00:16:01.400 --> 00:16:02.560
Two!

00:16:02.560 --> 00:16:03.480
Three!

00:16:03.480 --> 00:16:05.230
Four!

00:16:07.920 --> 00:16:11.200
And that's how it's done.

00:16:11.510 --> 00:16:12.960
Amazing.

00:16:13.990 --> 00:16:15.780
They're wiggling around.

00:16:17.980 --> 00:16:21.480
I faced a situation like 
this as a kid, too...

00:16:26.940 --> 00:16:27.810
Huh?

00:16:36.570 --> 00:16:38.480
I can't catch any of them.

00:16:42.500 --> 00:16:44.510
What the hell's your 
problem, Polar Bear?!

00:16:44.510 --> 00:16:46.190
Don't stand there laughing!

00:16:46.490 --> 00:16:48.730
Huh? I'm not laughing.

00:16:48.730 --> 00:16:50.900
Your mouth is laughing!

00:16:52.090 --> 00:16:54.610
It's just that my bottom lip is black.

00:16:55.890 --> 00:16:58.700
You're right, your mouth is closed.

00:16:58.700 --> 00:16:59.280
See?

00:17:00.030 --> 00:17:02.080
You're confusing, damn it.

00:17:14.130 --> 00:17:16.540
You are laughing, you ass!

00:17:17.050 --> 00:17:18.190
Couldn't help it.

00:17:22.240 --> 00:17:24.680
He may have been laughing then,

00:17:24.680 --> 00:17:27.060
but I can catch salmon like no other now.

00:17:30.230 --> 00:17:31.800
What the hell are you doing?

00:17:32.790 --> 00:17:34.310
Getting ready for a picnic.

00:17:34.310 --> 00:17:36.660
What the hell are you doing 
while I'm doing all the work?!

00:17:37.060 --> 00:17:39.900
Now, now, when you get hungry from

00:17:39.900 --> 00:17:41.320
catching all the salmon,

00:17:41.320 --> 00:17:43.200
I'll have lunch ready for you.

00:17:43.610 --> 00:17:44.910
Not bad, eh?

00:17:46.730 --> 00:17:49.380
Make something that'll fill me up.

00:17:56.280 --> 00:17:58.030
There aren't any salmon.

00:18:01.930 --> 00:18:03.600
What the hell are you doing?!

00:18:05.770 --> 00:18:09.100
I can't seem to get the hang 
of it like you, Mr. Grizzly.

00:18:11.150 --> 00:18:13.980
It totally looked like 
anyone could do it.

00:18:22.470 --> 00:18:24.140
Jeez, watch closely. 
This is how it's—

00:18:24.140 --> 00:18:26.790
I'm done. I'm gonna 
go eat bamboo grass.

00:18:27.830 --> 00:18:29.670
Don't wuss out so easily!

00:18:31.050 --> 00:18:34.630
But I'm tired, and I'm hungry.

00:18:34.630 --> 00:18:37.290
That's not the point!

00:18:37.290 --> 00:18:39.300
You're a bear, too, Polar Bear!

00:18:39.300 --> 00:18:41.340
Talk to him!

00:18:41.340 --> 00:18:45.350
Panda is happy if he has his 
bamboo and bamboo grass.

00:18:45.350 --> 00:18:45.980
Yup.

00:18:45.980 --> 00:18:47.600
What?!

00:18:47.600 --> 00:18:49.410
If you're a bear, hunt!

00:18:49.410 --> 00:18:51.520
Hunting is what makes you a bear!

00:18:59.990 --> 00:19:01.760
Bamboo shoot!

00:19:01.760 --> 00:19:03.470
I found some over there.

00:19:03.470 --> 00:19:07.350
This will probably make 
Panda want to hunt, too.

00:19:07.350 --> 00:19:08.650
I see.

00:19:15.410 --> 00:19:17.900
Huh? Salmon eat bamboo shoots?

00:19:17.900 --> 00:19:18.760
No.

00:19:19.770 --> 00:19:22.180
You're going to eat it, Panda.

00:19:23.750 --> 00:19:25.060
Panda.

00:19:25.470 --> 00:19:28.640
Grizzly's going to show 
you how to hunt.

00:19:29.910 --> 00:19:32.810
Hunting is what makes 
you a bear, right?

00:19:32.810 --> 00:19:36.320
Y-Yeah! Watch closely, Panda.

00:19:37.470 --> 00:19:40.060
First, you find your target.

00:19:47.440 --> 00:19:49.680
Don't ever take your eyes off of it.

00:19:52.370 --> 00:19:54.950
Predict how your enemy will move.

00:20:06.470 --> 00:20:08.430
How's that? Now you do it.

00:20:09.160 --> 00:20:10.540
So yummy!

00:20:10.540 --> 00:20:12.390
Quit stuffing your face!

00:20:13.130 --> 00:20:15.610
Come catch the swimming bamboo shoot!

00:20:15.610 --> 00:20:17.920
But bamboo shoots don't swim.

00:20:17.920 --> 00:20:19.130
I know, right?

00:20:19.130 --> 00:20:20.570
I know that!

00:20:20.570 --> 00:20:27.580
Danger

00:20:20.570 --> 00:20:27.580
Beware     of       Bears

00:20:28.640 --> 00:20:31.040
Don't be so mad, Mr. Grizzly.

00:20:31.440 --> 00:20:34.340
I'll give you my best bamboo grass.

00:20:34.340 --> 00:20:37.100
It's really good for your health, too.

00:20:40.270 --> 00:20:44.500
Don't be a picky eater yourself, 
and eat some salmon.

00:20:46.280 --> 00:20:47.430
Okay.

00:20:55.990 --> 00:20:57.570
How's the bamboo grass?

00:20:57.570 --> 00:21:01.430
Not that good. Isn't the salmon better?

00:21:02.390 --> 00:21:04.000
Not really.

00:21:06.230 --> 00:21:07.320
Something smells good!

00:21:07.840 --> 00:21:09.580
Coffee's ready.

00:21:09.580 --> 00:21:11.290
Thanks!

00:21:19.570 --> 00:21:21.680
It's so good.

00:21:21.680 --> 00:21:23.210
Yeah.

00:21:25.520 --> 00:21:28.000
It's good that you caught so much.

00:21:28.750 --> 00:21:30.250
Same for you.

00:21:31.560 --> 00:21:34.940
Very Popular

00:21:31.560 --> 00:21:34.940
Pasta Lunch

00:21:31.560 --> 00:21:34.940
Today's Pasta + Salad

00:21:40.120 --> 00:21:41.360
Hey, Panda!

00:21:42.020 --> 00:21:43.320
Over here!

00:21:44.220 --> 00:21:45.280
Welcome.

00:21:46.510 --> 00:21:49.650
The lunch pasta is a hit, thanks to you.

00:21:51.200 --> 00:21:52.240
Is this...

00:21:52.790 --> 00:21:54.210
Salmon and...

00:21:54.210 --> 00:21:55.620
...bamboo shoots?

00:21:56.790 --> 00:21:58.510
It's for all your hard work yesterday.

00:22:07.580 --> 00:22:12.000
Hey, Panda, I'll give you 
my bamboo shoots.

00:22:12.000 --> 00:22:14.910
I'll give you my salmon, Mr. Grizzly.

00:22:14.910 --> 00:22:17.190
It's not good to be such picky eaters.

00:22:17.710 --> 00:22:19.640
Don't sweat the small stuff.

00:22:19.640 --> 00:22:20.870
Yeah.

00:22:20.870 --> 00:22:22.010
Goodness...

00:22:22.010 --> 00:22:24.070
It's okay.

00:23:54.910 --> 00:24:24.480
Next Time

00:23:57.620 --> 00:23:59.650
Mr. Penguin, Mr. Penguin.

00:23:59.650 --> 00:24:00.970
What is it, Panda?

00:24:00.970 --> 00:24:05.540
Please tell me all the life lessons 
you have learned so far.

00:24:05.540 --> 00:24:06.860
When you're out drinking with others,

00:24:06.860 --> 00:24:09.170
and you're trying to 
eat the last piece,

00:24:09.170 --> 00:24:11.690
if you try to eat it as 
they're taking the plate,

00:24:11.690 --> 00:24:13.140
it won't be as awkward.

00:24:13.140 --> 00:24:16.020
That is a truly shallow life lesson.

00:24:16.020 --> 00:24:18.140
Polar Bear! Finish.

00:24:18.140 --> 00:24:21.020
Next time, on Polar Bear's Café Z.

00:24:21.020 --> 00:24:22.500
Don't put a "Z" on there.

00:24:21.060 --> 00:24:24.480
Rin Rin Deeply Moved! 
Panda's House!
Mr. Penguin's Proposal

00:24:22.500 --> 00:24:23.620
Enjoy!
